2026-07-27T03:30:07.2941109Z               "id": "642434c18da810e139eed3d59d8ac6e9efe49a88",
2026-07-27T03:30:07.2954767Z               "message": "Make AXFR honour the direct-DNS opt-out it was already documented under\n\n--no-direct-dns, the web tooltips, docs/configuration.md and both XML doc\ncomments all name AXFR among the checks that stop when direct DNS is off.\nZoneTransferCheck read only EnableAxfr, so it never did. Enabling the\ntransfer test in an environment that had opted out — including via the\n--restricted-network preset, which implies --no-direct-dns — still sent raw\nTCP/53 zone transfers at every authoritative nameserver.\n\nThe nameserver IPs it walks come from the configured resolver, so nothing\nupstream stopped it either: NsHostIps is fully populated whether or not\ndirect DNS is allowed. Add the same guard every sibling check already has.\n\nThat makes the existing wording true everywhere, so no help text or docs\nchange. The validator page's tooltip is the exception: AXFR is unreachable\nfrom there regardless — the page never sends enableAxfr — so listing it\namong the toggle's consequences invited the question this answers instead.\n\nTests cover all seven gated checks. The AXFR pair seeds the transfer verdict\ninto the resolver cache so the check reaches a finding offline, which is what\nmakes the skip assertion mean the gate fired rather than an empty context\nhaving nothing to report.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CsVVeUTFGF1xXBej8jFcY9",
2026-07-27T03:30:07.2965155Z               "timestamp": "2026-07-27T01:17:48Z",
2026-07-27T03:30:07.2965754Z               "tree_id": "d41f3284449661f792a6d4acaab2c19fb8a5b3dd",
2026-07-27T03:30:07.2966905Z               "url": "https://github.com/pkinerd/ednsv/commit/642434c18da810e139eed3d59d8ac6e9efe49a88"
2026-07-27T03:30:07.2967648Z             },
